# Warrant binding manifest (VER04 section 6, VER04j section 4.6) for
# code/specs/lzw.warrant.
#
# One line per Warrant operation: the public export that implements it, its
# host signature where the Warrant type is not the default one, and the
# deliberate faults the generated negative controls attack it with (VER04h
# section 6, VER04j section 4.8).
#
# compress: `compress(&[u8]) -> Vec<u8>`; the Warrant type `Bytes -> Bytes` is the
# default host signature, so no args=/ret=.
#
# decompress: `decompress(&[u8]) -> Result<Vec<u8>, String>`.  The Rust API has no
# error type: the error is a `String` message.  errors= maps the whole `String`
# (the path is `std::string`, the "variant" is the struct `String`, matched as
# `std::string::String { .. }`, as for wasm-leb128's `Leb128Error` struct) to the
# single Warrant case CORRUPT, so the claims separate "accepted with these bytes"
# from "rejected" and cannot see the message.  That is a limitation of what the
# public API makes observable, recorded in LZ01, not worked around.
#
# proofs_not_live=<reason> is the package's declaration that this operation's
# steps-bound obligation cannot be run: the Rust-subset front end refuses
# src/lib.rs (warrant-ir/tests/lzw_proofs.rs records its message).  Only an
# operation listed here may have a `not-live` entry in evidence/proof-manifest.json;
# `ca-assurance-report --check` rejects any other (VER04h section 9, check 18).
#
# exhaustive_budget is 2^24: decompress_three_bytes_rejected enumerates every
# 3-byte input (a U16 times a U8).  Together with the empty, 1-byte and 2-byte
# claims that is every input of length <= 3 (1 + 256 + 65,536 + 16,777,216 =
# 16,843,009).  The measured wall-clock cost is recorded in LZ01.
package lzw
revision 0.1.0
spec code/specs/lzw.warrant
output code/packages/rust/lzw/tests/generated/warrant_evidence.rs
seed 0x4c5a_5731_5f57_4152
property_cases 4096
fuzz_iterations 5000
negctl_fuzz_iterations 1000
exhaustive_budget 16777216

op compress export=compress faults=flip-result-bit,drop-last-result-byte proofs_not_live=frontend-refuses-lib
op decompress export=decompress errors=std::string/String=CORRUPT faults=flip-result-bit,drop-last-result-byte,missing-error proofs_not_live=frontend-refuses-lib
